  "question": {
    "text": "The mean and variance of a binomial distribution are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;respectively. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>243</mn></mfrac></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>or</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is equal to:"
